 {:semantic-assessment
  ["Change and RFC records require substantive lifecycle, affected-contract, compatibility/safety/profile/conformance and implementation links; accepted-for-implementation, implemented and stabilized remain different states. The eleven retained Core clauses are conditional instances of the same source-change producer, not extra tasks or evidence of underlying Core implementation."
   "Experiment lifecycle and per-use admission preserve explicit opt-in/artifact metadata, owner/scope/profile/default/expiry/rollback, compatibility-safe stable isolation, specialist review, on/off fixtures and reviewed expiry/exit. Export stability is visible to downstream consumers."
   "Stabilization and deprecation/removal preserve exact surfaces, conformance/negative history, compatibility/security/library review, replacement or explicit rationale, structured diagnostics and schedules, migration, support/tests until removal and explicit GOV4/GOV2 emergency exception. STD20 source/behavior/effect/capability/diagnostic/artifact/profile/conformance dimensions stay explicit."
   "Library admission preserves owners, export/profile/effect/capability/provider/unsafe metadata, positive/negative conformance, compatibility and signed release provenance; it does not implement the underlying library."
   "Security review/response preserve actual trust-boundary evidence, secret/taint/capability/unsafe/AI/supply-chain controls, residual risk, embargo/advisory/patch/backport/version/mitigation and compatibility exceptions. No human security decision is selected."
   "Target support requires actual tier/owner/profile/backend/runtime/debug/package/performance/security evidence and guarded removal. No target tier is selected by this allocation."
   "Namespace ownership/reservation/transfer/takeover remains accountable policy; Build/Auth mechanics consume that decision. Yank production records reasons/replacement/resolution while retaining locked rebuild identity and explicit emergency policy."
   "Build selection/install and registry admission consume governance/advisory/namespace/emergency inputs, preserve locks, deny undeclared authority and emit explainable policy or accept/reject/quarantine outcomes. Their broad existing fields supply concrete output entailment; summary wording alone is not treated as a witness."
   "Governance producers point to Release as a downstream consumer, never as a whole-task prerequisite. Declared artifact inputs remain conditional planning prerequisites; Open interfaces and nil required-output fields do not prove that artifacts or implementation already exist."],
